'''Ben Tennyson''', also known as '''Benzarro''',{{Refn|[[:File:And Then There Were None Voice Credits (1).png]]|group = credits}}<ref name=AT/> is an alternate and evil version of [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben Tennyson]].

==Appearance==
Benzarro has a stunted appearance, resembling a zombie. He wears a purple straitjacket with a "10" sewed on the chest, fourteen buckles on it and pants with patches. His body is green with blotches, he has purple eyes and a little purple hair, a long neck, pale yellow teeth, an under bite and animalistic toes.

Benzarro wears a purple Omnitrix called the [[Zombitrix]], which is located on a buckle by his elbow on the left straitjacket sleeve and not embedded in his flesh.{{Refn|[[:File:Zombitrix Not Embedded.png]]|group = DJW}}

==Personality==
Benzarro behaves very primitively, displaying ape-like body movements and dexterity in his human form. Instead of coherent speech, he only yells phrases like, "What we do now?" and "Ben smash!" as well as "Cousin mean". He also said "This fun!", "Stop running", and "Cousin dweeb!" while as [[Frankenstrike]]. He also headbutted his Omnitrix to transform,<ref name=AT/> further demonstrating his primitive behavior. However, Benzarro is not necessarily completely unintelligent, just backwards.{{Refn|[[:File:Benzarro Backwards.PNG]]|group = DJW}}

Despite being infected, Benzarro still has emotions.{{Refn|[[:File:Benzarro Has Emotions.png]]|group = DJW}}

==History==
===Background===
Benzarro originates from an alternate reality, where he is Patient 10 of a form of zombie outbreak that turns its victims into undead beings with Bizarro-ish traits.{{Refn|group = DJW|name = "Zarro"}} Benzarro was infected in the process of his creation, so he's never been normal.{{Refn|[[:File:Benzarro Patient 0.png]]|group = DJW|name = patient 0}} People from his world theorize that he's also Patient 0, the first zombie that caused the outbreak,{{Refn|[[:File:Patient 0 Caused the Outbreak.png]]|group = DJW}} but this has not been confirmed.{{Refn||group = DJW|name = patient 0}}

His reality's version of [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]] tried to cure him at one point, but in doing so, he became infected.{{Refn|[[:File:Benzarro Azmuth.PNG]]|group = DJW}}

===Omniverse===
Benzarro first appeared in ''[[And Then There Were None]]'', where he was among the evil Bens recruited by [[Eon]] and [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]] from across the [[multiverse]] and brought to the [[No Watch Timeline]] to wipe [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] out. [[Albedo]] and Benzarro, the latter as [[Frankenstrike]], chased No Watch Ben through [[Bellwood (Classic)|town]] until No Watch Ben was saved by [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben Prime]]. Later, in [[Los Soledad]], Benzarro was part of the fight between the good and evil Bens, as [[Snare-Oh]]. At the end of the episode, just like all the other Omnitrix wielders, he and his timeline were erased from spacetime by the [[Chronosapien Time Bomb]].

In ''[[And Then There Was Ben]]'', Benzarro was brought back into existence when No Watch Ben used [[Clockwork]] to suck the Time Bomb's ripple back in. Later, Benzarro turned into Frankenstrike again and fought [[Gwen 10 (Gweniverse)|Gwen 10]] as [[Wildvine (Classic)|Wildvine]], and was defeated when [[Vomit Man]] tried to swallow him by the head. At the end of the episode, he was sent back to his own reality by Clockwork.

==Powers and Abilities==
===Equipment===
[[File:TWB (430).png|thumb|Zombitrix]]
In battle, just like every other Ben, Benzarro relies on his [[Zombitrix|Omnitrix]]  to fight, which is also known as the Zombitrix.

==Weaknesses==
Although he is an undead being, Benzarro can be controlled by a [[Vladat]] via their [[Corruptura]]s.{{Refn|[[:File:Corrupturas & Zombies.png]]|group = DJW}}

